# See https://docs.github.com/articles/about-codeowners for syntax.
# Order matters — later matches take precedence, so the most specific rules
# are listed after the directory-wide rules.
#
# NOTE: the thyn-ai org has exactly one member today (@0xamlab) and no
# teams. Every entry below is that one real account, not a placeholder —
# replace with real teams (@thyn-ai/kernel-maintainers,
# @thyn-ai/python-wrapper-maintainers, @thyn-ai/ts-wrapper-maintainers) as
# soon as a second maintainer joins. Until then, do NOT turn on branch
# protection's "Require review from Code Owners" — GitHub blocks a PR author
# from approving their own PR, so a solo-owner CODEOWNERS with that setting
# on would make every PR unmergeable by the only person who can open one.

# Clean-room Mojo kernels and their exported C ABI.
/kernels/     @0xamlab

# Wrapper packages (Python: bm25-mojo, cclib-mojo; TypeScript: fuse-mojo).
/python/      @0xamlab
/typescript/  @0xamlab

# Differential test suites and seeded benchmarks are the parity guarantee —
# any change here gets flagged for deliberate review.
/tests/       @0xamlab
/benchmarks/  @0xamlab

# Toolchain pins: the Mojo compiler and every oracle version come from here.
/pixi.toml    @0xamlab
/pixi.lock    @0xamlab
/scripts/     @0xamlab

# Workflow files are as security-sensitive as the code they run.
/.github/     @0xamlab
